  message: "Filed during WI-hifol dogfood validation on 2026-05-19 self-analysis. After WI-hifol's WS-linker fix shipped (PR #3819, commit c926c2e5e3), INV-ronuf's quantitative claim moved 3 -> 0 (WS-origin duplicate file Symbols). The same self-analysis run revealed the IDENTICAL structural shape in js_module-linker-v1:\n\n5 paths with duplicate file-kind Symbols (origins = {javascript-v1, js-module-linker-v1}):\n  packages/htrac-frontend/src/components/item-detail.ts\n  packages/htrac-frontend/src/components/item-list.ts\n  packages/htrac-frontend/src/components/tracker-app.ts\n  packages/htrac-frontend/src/sw-register.ts\n  packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts\n\nFix pattern (per WI-hifol PR #3819): in the js_module linker's link_*() top-level, after collecting patterns/files, normalize each file_path via paths.normalize_path + prefix-strip against repo_root to mirror the orchestrator's algorithm byte-for-byte. Same five-line pattern that fixed websocket.\n\nStructural Fix Protocol cross-linker audit recommended: every linker that constructs file-kind Symbol ids from Path objects yielded by file-walk helpers needs the same path-normalization treatment. Audit list:\n  - websocket (fixed by WI-hifol PR #3819)\n  - js_module (this invariant)\n  - <audit remaining linkers in packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/>\n\nQuantitative claim: js_module duplicate file Symbols on self-analysis: 5 -> 0 expected after fix."  # 3b81
